From fac7ec0a1e64bd599b7f4fde2ecf744c8a67de85 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rodney Pantonial <rodneypantonial@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 04:41:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Nightly alarm: run the spaced cleanups one after another

With spacing, every cleanup had its own alarm at i x spacing minutes, so a slow one (Cleanup Inventory now sleeps) could still be running when the next one started, the first one waited for a 0-minute alarm, notices showed one by one and an exception no longer stopped the rest. Now the cleanups run in order as before: each next one starts Set Alarm Spacing sim-minutes after the previous one finished, the first runs at the alarm hour, notices are collected and shown as one message at the end, and an exception stops the night's remaining cleanups as before.

Spacing is capped so the whole run stays within 12 hours; a run still pending at the next alarm finishes first, in order, and a world load starts clean. Spacing 0 is the old single-frame run, unchanged. Existing saves get the default spacing: the game builds the settings object with its constructor and only overwrites the fields stored in the save.

Assisted with AI
